From ac9737463acf3a00fe278bace6cda370f2f58d69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:03:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc, shared: a WAN port found by Auto is pinned and never
 bridged into the LAN again

Stock auto WAN port detection finds the internet port by bridging every
candidate into br0 and running a DHCP client on the bridge; the closed
restore_auto_wanport() redid that at every boot and every WAN link loss, so
the ISP port carried LAN traffic for ~35-45 s each time (only DHCP and
RS/RA were filtered).

Once a port has carried the WAN it is pinned (nvram reaper_wanport,
rc/reaper_wanpin.c): stock's detected state is seeded from it at LAN start,
the boot and link-loss restore calls are skipped, wanduck stops relaunching
the search, and shared _eval refuses a `brctl addif` of the pinned port
while Auto is on and Dual WAN is off. Choosing a fixed port clears the pin;
`service start_reaper_wanredetect` forgets it and runs one detection.
Everything sits behind stock is_auto_wanport_enabled(), so AP mode, Dual
WAN, bonding, IPTV, static WAN and MAC clone are untouched. A new or reset
router still defaults to Auto.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
